# --- Unreal Engine generated ---
Binaries/
DerivedDataCache/
Intermediate/
Saved/
*.VC.db
*.VC.opendb
# Regenerable map lighting data. Must stay ignored: it is LFS-tracked as a
# *.uasset, so every rebuild would burn LFS quota permanently.
*_BuiltData.uasset
# NOTE: no bare `Build/` rule. Build/ holds packaging *inputs* (platform icons,
# provisioning) that must be committed; real build output is already covered by
# Intermediate/ and Binaries/.

# --- Visual Studio / Rider / IDEs ---
.vs/
.vsconfig
*.sln
*.suo
*.opensdf
*.sdf
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- Packaging ---
Builds/
Packaged/

# --- OS cruft ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Local-only ---
*.log
.claude/settings.local.json

# --- Prototype build artifacts ---
# Matches the extensionless binary clang++ emits with `-o test_blocksignal` as
# well as the .exe Windows produces; the negation keeps the sources tracked.
# Verify after editing: `git check-ignore -v Prototypes/TrackSpline/test_trackspline`
Prototypes/**/test_*
!Prototypes/**/test_*.cpp
Prototypes/**/*.o
Prototypes/**/*.obj
Prototypes/**/*.pdb
# The telemetry recorder is a tool rather than a test_*, so the rule above
# misses it; its recordings are machine-specific captures, not source.
Prototypes/NL2Telemetry/record
Prototypes/NL2Telemetry/record.exe
Prototypes/NL2Telemetry/calibrate
Prototypes/NL2Telemetry/calibrate.exe
Prototypes/NL2Csv/compare
Prototypes/NL2Csv/compare.exe
Prototypes/**/telemetry*.csv

# --- NL2 track imports and park files (scratch) ---
# Working directories for NoLimits 2 content: .nl2park files and the CSV spline
# exports fed to Prototypes/NL2Csv. Kept out of the repo because third-party
# park content is not ours to redistribute, and recreations of real rides would
# breach the no-real-ride-designs rule in CLAUDE.md. Commit an original,
# self-authored test track if one is ever actually needed as a fixture.
Prototypes/NL2Csv/Tracks/
NL2/

# Brand pack. The source machinery — templates, build scripts, SVG marks, the
# built HTML pages and the 4K loading-screen exports — is kept locally but is
# not part of the codebase. The five figures the README and Docs/ actually embed
# ARE tracked, because a public README with four broken images is worse than no
# brand pack at all.
#
# The measurement driver that used to live at Brand/src/gen_data.cpp was NOT
# branding and did not go with it: it is Prototypes/TrackSpline/reference_figures.cpp,
# and it is what makes REFERENCE_LAYOUT.md's canonical numbers reproducible.
Brand/*
!Brand/github/
Brand/github/*
!Brand/github/*.png
